    "done_when": "SensorMapping.efm_index in imas_ambix/gs/geometry.py is typed int or None, and the type-6 mapping built in imas_ambix/data/geometry_adapter.py carries None in place of -1, so a consumer that forgets the guard fails with a TypeError rather than reading the last positioned loop. The existing guards stay. Comments at imas_ambix/gs/geometry.py and imas_ambix/data/geometry_adapter.py describe the None sentinel that the code now holds. A new test asserts every type-6 mapping's efm_index is None and that indexing a loop list with it raises TypeError. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set) or all_debug, with IMAS_ALAMBIC_MAP_PATH=/home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-ambix/maps-staging/jtmm-differential-loop-consumers, uv run --no-sync pytest tests/data/test_jt60sa_machine_map.py tests/gs/test_operator.py tests/gs/test_operator_differential_loops.py tests/gs/test_artifact_geometry.py tests/spine_bench/test_transform_geometry_source.py tests/spine_bench/test_machine_artifact_arm.py exits 0, captured once to a log with the revision and command on its first lines, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0.",
